WEBVTT

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.640
Present Day

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.590
Present Time

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:23.340
And you don't seem to understand

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:28.540
A shame you seemed an honest man

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:33.290
And all the fears you hold so dear

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.560
Will turn to whisper in your ear

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:41.960
And you know what they say might hurt you

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.430
And you know that it means so much

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:49.190
And you don't even feel a thing

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:54.850
I am falling, I am fading

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:58.970
I have lost it all

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:26.990
I am falling, I am fading, I am drowning

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.630
Help me to breathe

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:34.840
I am hurting, I have lost it all

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.380
I am losing

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:41.580
Help me to breathe

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:14.270
I don't need parents. Humans are all alone.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:18.440
They're not connected to anyone at all.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.340
How did it go?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.300
Lain's acting funny.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.100
It's nothing new, but still...

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.060
No, it's perfectly normal.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.770
Huh? What're you talking about?

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:22.610
Mika, watch your tone with your father.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.660
Is she right?

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.500
Yes.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.460
Shit! Shit!

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:30.560
Shit!

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.440
Shit! Shit!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.660
What do you want?!

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.450
What's going on?!

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.080
Shit!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.920
SHIT!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.260
Gotcha.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.360
We have homeroom next hour, right? Is that lucky, or what?

00:06:34.360 --> 00:06:37.830
Don't you think it's strange that they called a special staff meeting?

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:41.160
Do you think it's true, then?

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:43.290
What?

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.710
They say a high school senior committed suicide.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.000
S-Suicide?

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:52.470
It's not just at our school, either.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:56.090
Somebody jumped off the roof of their apartment building a while ago, too.

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.640
Hey, Lain.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:04.890
Sorry. What is it?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.650
I guess Lain wouldn't know anything about it...

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:14.860
The suicide, you mean?

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:16.490
You know about that?

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:17.740
Really?

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:21.290
I've just heard a little about it, that's all.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.290
Where?

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.040
The Wired.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:30.130
Right, you must've gotten the hang of your new Navi by now.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.880
You'll have to show it to me sometime.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:35.720
Sure. But I'm modifying it a little right now.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:39.640
Modifying it? I didn't know you were into that hacking stuff.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.180
You know, you've changed lately.

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:47.350
Really? You think so?

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.940
She has?

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.360
Yeah. I can't put my finger on it.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.160
So, what sort of rumors have you heard in the Wired?

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.660
Well... That's it's some kind of game.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.660
A game? A network game, you mean?

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:10.170
I don't really know. I don't play those.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:15.260
But they say that all the dead kids were hooked on it.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.180
Guys sure like that stuff...

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:21.600
A game, huh? But why?

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.760
I...

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.980
Hey, don't wolf down food like that! You'll choke!

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.270
I'm okay.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:33.320
You mind if I go home?

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:36.440
Hey, you don't need to ask our permission or anything.

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:37.570
You have plans?

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:40.700
I want to get home and put my Navi back together.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.580
It's still in bits and pieces.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.410
You prefer a machine to your friends, huh?

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:49.080
Cut it out, Juri! Don't talk like that!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.210
I'm not accusing her of anything.

00:08:51.210 --> 00:08:54.090
Once you're done, you'll have to show us, Lain.

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.670
Sure.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:01.010
Sorry.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.100
She has changed.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:13.770
I'm sorry!

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:15.780
Here.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:20.450
No, it was my fault.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:24.580
Sorry!

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:42.130
Log in. Lain.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.140
Authorized.

00:09:44.140 --> 00:09:45.970
Mail.

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.390
Voice mail.

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.570
Hello, Lain.

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:01.860
I couldn't figure out the answer to your question by myself,

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:04.490
so I asked a colleague at the lab about it.

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:09.620
If that really is a Psyche processor that you have,

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:15.710
then you should probably set the oscillation to "variable" like you thought.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:21.300
Navi motherboards are designed to work with just about anything,

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.680
but you might run into some glitches.

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:25.850
Good luck.

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:28.810
If you need anything else, just ask.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.240
JJ!

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.320
Yeah?

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.020
You know anything about that net game that all the kids are playing?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.130
Oh, you mean Phantoma?

00:10:57.130 --> 00:11:01.590
Forget about it. An adult like you wouldn't be into that.

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:05.050
Right, Lain?

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.720
No way...

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:11.720
Damn, are my ears playing tricks on me already?

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:49.260
I... I quit already!

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:50.850
Leave me out of it!

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:52.700
This isn't the Wired!

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:55.540
Why? Why is this happening?!

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:58.710
Wait, don't run.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:07.130
Who are you?!

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:12.680
Are you a PK, too? Help me!

00:13:12.680 --> 00:13:15.060
I can't go where you are.

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.390
What's going on?!

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.870
Stop screwing around!

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:50.010
Bullet charge! Gauge 5!

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:53.510
Die!

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:58.720
Die!

00:13:58.720 --> 00:13:59.600
Die!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.230
Die!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:01.940
Die!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:02.980
Die!

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:03.690
Die!

00:14:08.660 --> 00:14:09.580
Die!

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:10.610
Die!

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:11.280
Die!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:13.110
Die!

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:13.860
Die!

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:14.780
Die!

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:15.570
Die!

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:27.060
I was scared, that's all.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:34.170
I didn't know it was just a little girl. It's not my fault.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.450
I didn't even know her.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:43.340
Phantoma is a game with a dedicated client application

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:47.310
that lets you fight in the Wired.

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:53.950
I downloaded the app from an illegal server to play it a little while ago.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:16:00.490
For us, it had a dungeon-style action game interface,

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:05.130
but I guess it had somehow gotten linked

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.200
to a tag game played by kindergartners.

00:16:15.790 --> 00:16:17.610
You have mail.

00:16:18.190 --> 00:16:19.440
Open it.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:25.080
Hey, Lain. I didn't know you were into stuff like Phantoma.

00:16:27.170 --> 00:16:30.250
I checked around, but didn't find out much.

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:35.550
Anyway, the basic game isn't all that unusual in the Wired,

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:38.430
so my guess is that they just modified that.

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:43.350
The problem is the part that lets the programs connect to each other.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.270
It looks like there's some kind of weird hole in the protocol.

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:51.650
My buddies and I think that this may be the work of the Knights, too.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.620
Knights...

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:02.870
Lain?

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:09.290
Looks like you and the Wired are getting along just fine now.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.250
Yeah.

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:14.960
Let me give you one little warning.

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:16.170
Huh?

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:21.470
When it's all said and done, the Wired

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.470
is just a medium for communication and the transfer of information.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:26.930
You mustn't confuse it with the real world.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:35.190
Do you understand what I'm warning you about?

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.780
You're wrong.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.860
Huh?

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:47.620
The border between the two isn't all that clear.

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:56.090
I'll be able to enter it soon.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:18:01.220
In full range. Full motion. I'll translate myself into it.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:06.140
Even with a top of the line civilian Navi, you couldn't...

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:10.140
I can do it. I've modified mine.

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:13.600
A Psyche processor, huh?

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:14.610
But...

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:19.480
Don't worry. I'm still me.

00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:22.030
Sometimes I wonder.

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.300
I waited for you for hours!

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:55.300
Why? Why didn't you come?!

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:04.140
Damn you! Damn you! Damn you!

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:05.880
Damn you!

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:12.620
This mail is a message of happiness!

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:17.040
By receiving this, you'll be happier than anyone else!

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:23.050
In other words, the Knights do not physically exist,

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:26.760
but are rather a thought itself that occurs within the Wired.

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:31.930
They can be thought of as a religion that is spreading through the Wired.

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:34.690
Would you go out with me?

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:37.730
If you already have a boyfriend, I apologize.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:44.280
If you love him, I'll give up on you. But if...

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:51.160
Please browse code J946@5488AA97464.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:57.560
Whoever gets this mail, please help me, whoever you are.

00:19:57.560 --> 00:20:02.920
You may not believe this, but I'm always being followed.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.970
Lain, why won't you come here?

00:21:04.530 --> 00:21:06.230
Go away.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:17.870
Go away!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:46.440
Intruder interrupted.

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:35.960
nan no tsumi mo nai hazu na no ni

00:22:31.530 --> 00:22:35.960
Although I must be innocent,

00:22:35.960 --> 00:22:39.870
nanraka no batsu wo uketeru

00:22:35.960 --> 00:22:39.870
now I am punished.

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:46.170
jibun de maita tane de mo nai no ni

00:22:40.300 --> 00:22:46.170
I wasn't the one who sowed those seeds, but nevertheless

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:53.080
sakimidareta hana tsumasareru

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:53.080
I have to pull up the flowers that bloomed from them.

00:22:59.630 --> 00:23:04.270
shiranai koto to mo ienai ga

00:22:59.630 --> 00:23:04.270
I can't say I didn't know about it,

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:08.720
katabou katsuida oboe wa nai

00:23:04.270 --> 00:23:08.720
but I don't remember taking any part in it.

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:14.910
jiyuu wo takaku kawasareta ki mo suru ga

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:14.910
I think my freedom cost me dearly,

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:22.150
kokoro made yasuku utta oboe wa nai

00:23:15.440 --> 00:23:22.150
but I don't remember selling my soul so cheaply.

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:30.200
Hey Hey kutabatte osaraba suru made

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:30.200
Hey hey, until I die and say farewell...

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:40.110
Hey Hey dare no te ni mo kakaranai

00:23:31.220 --> 00:23:40.110
Hey hey... no one can touch me.

00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:45.720
tooi yoru wo urotsuiteiru

00:23:41.630 --> 00:23:45.720
You probably don't know

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:53.430
shiranai darou eien no narazu monotachi wo

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:53.430
the eternal outlaws prowling in the distant night.
